f] → 020H part 2 → 020D2 → [USER-GATE-A] (12 implementation slices + 1 mid-chain human-input gate + 1 terminal gate, matching WP-SCP-020 §3 canonical sequence verbatim). Track 2 (021): 021B → 021C → 021D → 021E → [USER-GATE-C] (4 implementation slices + 1 terminal gate). Concurrent-dispatch limit: 4 active Codex sessions across both tracks. `pyproject.toml` partition: Track 1 owns `[tool.scp.federation]` and adds `scp-policy-check` to `[project.scripts]`; Track 2 owns `[project.optional-dependencies.mcp]` and adds `scp-mcp-server` to `[project.scripts]`. `docs/STATUS.md` excluded from all slice scope_boundary globs | ACCEPTED | WP-SCP-021 §scope statement declares the tracks independent; serial execution would defer MCP availability for ~2× wall-clock without quality gain. Concurrent dispatch within rate-limit envelope per `four-tier-dispatch-field-report-2026-04-22.md`. Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.4. Track 1 sequence corrected in v0.2 (R1 fix-round) to match WP-SCP-020 §3 canonical ordering — earlier draft omitted 020K and inverted 020D2 placement |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md-80-| D-028 | 2026-04-28 | SCP adopts D-048 / ADR-016 Design Parity Build Method (DPBM) as a contract input for any SCP slice that produces designed visual output. Layered amendment to four-tier dispatch — prototype + flows + design principles enter the contract layer the build is bound to. Enforcement-injection mechanism per `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.6: visual-output slices' dispatch packages MUST include a \"DPBM contract\" subsection naming prototype path, flow diagram, and design-principles reference; orchestrator verifies subsection presence before launching the review pass; absence is treated as a CRIT finding. Within WP-SCP-022 itself no slices match the DPBM \"applies\" criteria (workflow / Rego / MCP-server / CI work, no visual output); D-028 is forward-looking. WP-SCP-024 estate cascade inherits D-028; FLA, AC